  body: "# Prescribed disease and occupation pairing\n\n## Authored interpretation\n\nThe source links prescribed
    diseases or injuries to occupations laid down in legislation, distinguishing prescription from the diagnosis
    and attribution questions.\n\n## Scope and exceptions\n\nA diagnosis alone does not establish the required prescribed
    occupation or employed-earner connection. The source points to a possible industrial-accident route where prescription
    is absent, subject to its own conditions. Disease names, group letters and numbers and versions must be retained.\n\
    \n## Inspected passages\n\n- [DMG 67001, PDF page 3](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/693acc2f33c7ace9c4a4202e/dmg-v-11-ch-67.pdf#page=3).\n\
    - [DMG 67002, PDF page 3](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/693acc2f33c7ace9c4a4202e/dmg-v-11-ch-67.pdf#page=3).\n\
    - [DMG 67003, PDF page 3](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/693acc2f33c7ace9c4a4202e/dmg-v-11-ch-67.pdf#page=3).\n\
    - [DMG 67007, PDF page 4](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/693acc2f33c7ace9c4a4202e/dmg-v-11-ch-67.pdf#page=4).\n\
    - [DMG 67009, PDF page 4](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/693acc2f33c7ace9c4a4202e/dmg-v-11-ch-67.pdf#page=4).\n\
    \n## Additional context\n\n- [Context: chapter 67, PDF page 4](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/693acc2f33c7ace9c4a4202e/dmg-v-11-ch-67.pdf#page=4).\n\
    \n## Evidence and review status\n\nIndependent experimental interpretation of captured DWP guidance, not an
    official DWP document. Definitions and semantic associations are model-assisted proposals awaiting specialist
    review. No individual entitlement decision, medical conclusion, award calculation or executable rule is provided.\n\
    \nSource observation, listing-page update, printed revision, legal event and claimant-event dates are separate.
    Current legal applicability is unresolved. Page numbers are one-based PDF positions; machine extraction may
    damage reading order, characters and footnotes. No visual PDF or specialist acceptance is claimed.\n\n- `dmg-vol11-ch67`:
    PDF `3c7414b2ec9ba0ec4073199a063a97072e1bf2c670f1620e241884a39b7e201a`; extracted pages `f6415f436f2f1eea4febaa9f82fbd0ad34a6fc754ce3c59c24fd10311ba0ad12`;
    acquired `2026-09-15T19:45:34.130077Z`.\n"
  resource: https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/693acc2f33c7ace9c4a4202e/dmg-v-11-ch-67.pdf#page=3
  semantic_relations:
  - target: term/prescribed-disease-presumption
    predicate: http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related
    rationale: The source distinguishes prescription from statutory presumptions connecting disease with
      employment.
    evidence:
    - page: page/dmg-vol11-ch67/0006
      quote: "67017 The onus of proving that a person is or was suffering from a PD and that the remaining conditions\n\
        for award of benefit under the PD provisions are satisfied rests on the claimant. But there are statutory\n\
        provisions which can operate in the claimant's favour. These relate to\n\n\n1. the satisfaction of the conditions
        for an REA award in pneumoconiosis cases (see DMG Chapter 71)\n\n\n2. the satisfaction of the condition
        that the PD is due to the nature of the employment (see DMG 67101\net seq)\n\n\n3. determining the date
        of onset (see DMG 67249)\n\n\n4. recrudescence (see DMG 67141 et seq)."
      locator: DMG 67017
  - target: term/industrial-accident-question
    predicate: http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related
    rationale: Some IA provisions apply to prescribed-disease claims with modifications; this is a scoped
      association, not wholesale equivalence.
    evidence:
    - page: page/dmg-vol11-ch67/0006
      quote: "67016 Many of the statutory provisions governing accident claims apply without change to PD claims.\n\
        Some apply with modifications, and others do not apply at all. Guidance on the adaptations and\nmodifications
        is at DMG 67017 - 67038.\n\n\n\nBurden of proof"
      locator: DMG 67016
    - page: page/dmg-vol11-ch67/0006
      quote: "67021 The benefits payable for a PD and the general conditions for such benefits are the same as those\n\
        \nfor injury by IA1. So the guidance in DMG Chapter 66 regarding benefits in respect of accidents applies\n\
        also to PD claims, subject to modifications in DMG 67022 et seq.\n\n\n                                 \
        \                                          1 SS CB Act 92, s 109(1)(a) & (b)"
      locator: DMG 67021
